            <ArticleTitle>An unexpected cause of anaphylaxis: potato.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>149-52</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Immediate reactions against contact to raw potato has been reported in adults with generally being in the form of an oral contact dermatitis or contact urticaria, but it may also manifest as rhinitis symptoms, wheezing or even anaphylaxis. Cooked or raw potato allergy has been rarely reported in children as some is being immediate and others being late reactions, and it usually results from ingestion. Herein, we report two cases with a background of allergic diseases developed anaphylaxis one with cooked potato and the other one with raw potato.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
